<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernardo Houssay</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1887">1887</a>–<a href="/years/1971">1971</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernardo Houssay was an Argentine physiologist who shared the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-prize">Nobel Prize</a> in Physiology or Medicine in 1947 for discovering the part played by hormones of the pituitary gland in the metabolism of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a>. He was the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> American laureate in the sciences, and he founded institutions that shaped scientific research in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>, including the national research council, CONICET.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bernardo-houssay.jpg" alt="Bernardo Houssay" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Desconocido · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bernardo_Alberto_Houssay.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
